From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 09:17:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DOS: INT 2Dh (AMIS) and the provider DOS-UTF8/CLIPBRD: UTF-8
 text of the DOS clipboard API

AMIS 3.6 on INT 2Dh with one provider for now, "DOS-UTF8" "CLIPBRD": a DOS program that asks
(AL=10h BX=65001) gets the text of INT 2Fh AX=1703h/1704h/1705h (formats CF_TEXT, CF_OEMTEXT) as
UTF-8 instead of the OEM code page, so that characters outside the code page survive. The mode is
per process (the current PSP) and ends with it; AL=11h reads it. The provider is present only when
the DOS clipboard API is enabled (dos clipboard api=true). SDL2 and Windows hosts (CF_UNICODETEXT);
other hosts keep the OEM path. Specification: docs/UTF8CLIPBOARD.md of github.com/unxed/go2dos.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015ykCKPSoMUrfqu87pXBAug
